OL,3,GNEWSAEverything you need to know about
OL,4,AHop Tu Naa
OL,5,
OL,6,FWhile 31 October is widely known as
OL,7,FHalloween, people on the Isle of Man
OL,8,Fwill be marking Hop Tu Naa.
OL,10,FAn evening where children swap pumpkins
OL,11,Ffor turnips, dress up, knock on doors,
OL,12,Fand sing about "Jinnie the Witch" all
OL,13,Fwhile collecting sweets along the way.
OL,15,FHop Tu Naa is traditionally considered
OL,16,Fthe Celtic New Year, celebrating the
OL,17,Fsafe gathering of the harvest and a
OL,18,Fsign that good preparations had been
OL,19,Fmade for the coming winter.
OL,23,APub: 17-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
